# ── build output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.o
*.obj
*.exe
*.out
inop
build/
probe
probe.exe

# ── KEY MATERIAL — never commit these ───────────────────────────────────
# Wheel files and key sheets are the secret. Committing them to a public
# repo is the exact failure the whole design is meant to avoid: it hands an
# analyst the machine's wiring and the day's settings in one place.
inop_wheels.txt
inop_keysheet.txt
inop.settings
*.settings
*.keysheet
setup/

# The GUI Save Setup panel writes master_key into JSON (to_json() in
# gui_config_store.cpp). Every one of those files lands in setup/, which
# the line above already covers whole — this states the rule that line
# only implies, so moving kDir cannot quietly start publishing key
# material. *.json is deliberately not blanket-ignored: CMakePresets.json
# and vcpkg.json are tracked and belong in the repo.
setup/*.json

# ── generated benchmark output ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Timing columns are machine/run-specific — committing them just churns the
# diff on every re-run for no benefit.
benchmark.csv

# ── editor / OS noise ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ── local backup mirrors ────────────────────────────────────────────────
/WorldEngine-backup.git/

# ── untracked by intent, now by rule ────────────────────────────────────
# Both were untracked by convention only, which is not a rule. maria.txt
# is the roadmap. .claude/ holds local absolute paths and permission
# grants; it is currently caught by a machine-local global ignore file
# that does not travel with a clone, so the repo has to say it too.
maria.txt
.claude/

# ── working notes, not a published document ─────────────────────────────
# DESIGN.md is a scratchpad for reasoning in progress, not a deliverable.
# Untracked deliberately by the owner on this branch (it had been tracked
# since the project started). Nothing written here should cite it.
DESIGN.md
